# Keeps local build output out of the image.
#
# Not a size optimisation. COPY would otherwise pull your machine's bin/ and obj/ into the build,
# where they sit on top of what the container restores - stale assemblies and a project.assets.json
# describing paths that do not exist inside the image. That produces build failures that look like
# code errors, and it only happens on a machine that has built locally, so it is the kind of thing
# that works in CI and fails for you.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Not needed by the API image, and node_modules in particular is tens of thousands of files that
# would be sent to the Docker daemon as build context for no reason.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
.git/
.vs/
.vscode/
